    <h2 id="manufacturing">Manufacturing and Quality Considerations</h2>
    <p>Cosmetic aerosol hair products require controlled manufacturing environments, precision filling equipment, and strict quality systems. Consistency in fill weight, pressure, spray rate, and valve performance is essential for both safety and brand reputation.</p>
    <p>Quality control extends beyond formulation to include can integrity, valve crimping accuracy, propellant purity, and finished product testing under multiple temperature conditions.</p>

    <h3>Why Aerosol Hair Products Fail Without Process Control</h3>
    <p>In industrial settings, aerosol hair product failures are rarely caused by a single factor. Instead, they result from cumulative deviations in filling accuracy, crimp quality, propellant purity, or formulation–packaging compatibility. Even technically sound hair spray formulations can fail if manufacturing controls are inadequate.</p>
    <p>Professional aerosol manufacturing relies on validated processes, documented quality systems, and repeatable performance metrics, not only on ingredient selection.</p>

    <table>
    <tr><th>Critical Manufacturing Controls</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Valve crimp integrity and pressure retention</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Spray rate and particle size consistency</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Stability across temperature and transport conditions</td></tr>
    </table></div>

